From 3d270d3aa403439f796df2796157201c895e1ebe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 20:06:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] connect: convert to string based connections

Qt4 can not connect to a pointer to member function or to a functor,so
every such connect in the tree becomes a SIGNAL() string connection,
going through the connectFunctor*() helpers where the receiver is a
lambda or a plain(non slot) member function.

The 3 argument Qt5 form connect( sender,signal,functor ) ties the
connection lifetime to the sender,so those call sites pass the sender as
the context object;the 4 argument form keeps the context it had.

Two receivers stayed real slots because a string based connection needs
the slot argument types to spell out the same as the signal ones:
sirikali::trayClicked() and checkforupdateswindow::add()/doneUpdating().

Outside the GUI:

- src/3rdParty/tasks/task.hpp: the two QThread::finished connects become
  string based ones and Task::progress routes its functor through a real
  slot on Qt4.
- src/siripolkit: zuluPolkit gains Q_OBJECT with start() and
  gotConnection() as real slots,which also lets main() drop the manual
  single shot timer.
- src/sirikali_cppcryptfs: uses the connectFunctor*() helpers.
- utils/network_access_manager.hpp drops QMetaObject::Connection(Qt 5.0),
  the carrier object returned by connectFunctor*() is deleted to break
  the connection instead.
- utils/single_instance.hpp loses its Qt < 5.4 Q_OBJECT variant of
  details::exec,singleShotFunctor() covers every version and the header
  is not moc'ed by any target.

QProcess::ProcessError and QProcess::ExitStatus are registered as meta
types while here.  A queued connection resolves the argument types of
the signal through QMetaType::type() and silently refuses to deliver
what it can not resolve,and Qt only started registering those two when
Q_ENUM replaced Q_ENUMS in Qt 5.5.  utils/qprocess.hpp connects both of
them queued.

